{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aea6dede398a659c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9001-E001\n3\ttitle: Surface InferenceService deployment status in Dashboard model serving views\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9001\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 8\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Surface InferenceService deployment status in Dashboard model serving views\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers deployment status visibility for KServe InferenceService\n34\tmodels directly in the RHOAI Dashboard. Data scientists see at a glance whether\n35\teach deployed model is Ready, Progressing, or Failed, can drill into the\n36\tunderlying condition messages and recent Kubernetes events for failed or\n37\tprogressing deployments, see status updates within 30 seconds without a manual\n38\tpage reload, and filter and sort the deployed models list by status. This\n39\tremoves the need for Dashboard users to run `oc get inferenceservice` or read\n40\tKubernetes events to determine deployment health.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Derive a display status (Ready, Progressing, Failed) for each deployed\n45\t  InferenceService from the InferenceService CR status conditions and Kubernetes\n46\t  events, as exposed by the KServe InferenceService CRD\n47\t  (serving.kserve.io/v1beta1).\n48\t- Display the derived status for each deployed model in the Dashboard model\n49\t  serving views.\n50\t- Add a status detail view that shows the underlying condition messages and\n51\t  recent events for a failed or progressing deployment.\n52\t- Ensure the displayed status reflects the actual InferenceService state within\n53\t  30 seconds of a change, without requiring a manual page reload.\n54\t- Add filter and sort controls for the deployed models list based on status.\n55\t- Out of scope: alerting or notifications on status transitions, status\n56\t  history / timeline views, and ModelMesh deployments (KServe InferenceService\n57\t  only).\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- Given a deployed InferenceService in each of Ready, Progressing, and Failed\n62\t  states, the Dashboard model serving views display the corresponding status\n63\t  for each deployed model.\n64\t- Given a failed or progressing deployment, opening the status detail view\n65\t  shows the underlying InferenceService condition messages and recent\n66\t  Kubernetes events.\n67\t- Given a change in the InferenceService state, the displayed status in the\n68\t  Dashboard reflects the new state within 30 seconds, without a manual page\n69\t  reload.\n70\t- Given a list of deployed models with mixed statuses, the user can filter the\n71\t  list by status and sort it by status.\n72\t- The status derivation is verified against the KServe InferenceService CR\n73\t  status conditions (e.g. Ready, PredictorReady) and Kubernetes events for each\n74\t  supported condition state, confirming the Dashboard correctly maps the\n75\t  passive KServe-provided state to the displayed status.\n76\t\n77\t## HLR Traceability\n78\t\n79\t- HLR-1 (P0): Users see a deployment status (Ready, Progressing, Failed) for\n80\t  each deployed model in the Dashboard model serving views.\n81\t- HLR-2 (P0): Users can open a status detail view showing the underlying\n82\t  condition messages and recent events for a failed or progressing deployment.\n83\t- HLR-3 (P1): Displayed status reflects the actual InferenceService state\n84\t  within 30 seconds of a change, without a manual page reload.\n85\t- HLR-4 (P2): Users can filter and sort the deployed models list by status.\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8a3c47bc999a55e","agent_id":"a22624d9becab0bb2","session_id":"3262f4f3-4bb8-476b-b267-edc8e3b37f2e","uuid":"3e5c47d9-0b9b-4132-8c60-c776e9d8fe09","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:07:45.463Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aea6dede398a659c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9001 decomposition"}
