nflux-onboarding/license-validation/repo-onboarding\n43\tepics so rules 7/8/10 are moot. Critical path length 2 matches the S-size\n44\theuristic (1-2). No conditional branch files exist, and no branch epic appears\n45\tin any main-plan dependency list. No data/artifact dependency is missing from\n46\tthe DAG: E002 consumes only the shipped feature behavior, which is captured by\n47\tthe Rule 11 edge and the technical-review AC.\n48\t\n49\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n50\t\n51\tE001 (Dashboard / RHOAI Dashboard) and E002 (Documentation / RHOAI Dashboard)\n52\tare separate epics along the component axis. No epic bundles multiple teams.\n53\tNo scope duplication: E001 builds the status UI, E002 documents it — neither\n54\trebuilds the other's work, and they are not two presentation modes of one\n55\tsurface. Work-product types are cleanly separated (code in E001, content\n56\tauthoring in E002), satisfying the type-mixing boundary rule. Neither epic\n57\tappears oversized; E001 is a bounded extension of existing model serving views.\n58\t\n59\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n60\t\n61\tBoth epics are correctly typed Implementation. E001 produces a concrete code\n62\tartifact; E002 produces documentation content with `implementation_type:\n63\tdocs-authoring`. No Investigation epics exist, which is justified: the\n64\tstrategy's open questions state \"None blocking,\" corroborated by the KServe\n65\tarchitecture context. No `gated_by`/`gate_failure_impact` fields are set, and\n66\tnone are needed.\n67\t\n68\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n69\t\n70\tBoth epics are Implementation type and correctly carry the 9-signal\n71\t`ai_signals` field (not `investigation_signals`). E001's signal values are\n72\tconsistent with the strategy content and architecture context — `open_questions:\n73\t1` matches the strategy's \"None blocking,\" `architecture_claims: 1` matches the\n74\tKServe architecture context substantiating the CR status conditions claim.\n75\tE002's `human_process_gates: -1` is justified by the docs editorial/technical\n76\treview process (Rule 24). Rationales in both ai-signals files match the\n77\tfrontmatter values and are substantive.\n78\t\n79\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n80\t\n81\tE001 has five testable Given-state ACs covering display, detail view, 30-second\n82\tfreshness, filter/sort, and passive-component validation against the KServe CR\n83\tstatus conditions. E002 has three testable ACs including the rule-mandated\n84\ttechnical review against the implemented feature (Rule 24 for docs-authoring).\n85\tNo replacement/konflux-chain epics exist, so no other rule-mandated ACs apply.\n86\tNo AC is an external schedule constraint, and no epic body references sibling\n87\tepics by draft ID.\n88\t\n89\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n90\t\n91\tAll strategy scope is covered: HLR-1..HLR-4 in E001's scope and ACs, HLR-5 in\n92\tE002 (including filter/sort coverage and stale-screenshot updates in scope).\n93\tThe strategy's out-of-scope list is carried into E001's scope. The docs\n94\trequirement (HLR-5) has a docs-authoring epic. Strategy-level context is not\n95\tdropped: the 30-second soft real-time risk is carried into the summary's\n96\tHealth Warnings and an E001 AC; the missing-strategy-sections caveat is\n97\tdocumented. The problem statement's user pain (Pending-for-an-hour support\n98\tcases) is reflected in E001's description.\n99\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af14078c947de3ad","agent_id":"a3caada836d5a2dbb","session_id":"3262f4f3-4bb8-476b-b267-edc8e3b37f2e","uuid":"aed049cd-55e3-47fa-a330-8c1ebfe58376","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:09:51.685Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b00eb648915d90ee","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9001 decomposition"}
